  "result": "Quiz 0002, \"Workflows, agents and who owns the control flow\", is ready in `quizzes/0002.json`. Its key is in `keys/0002.json`. It has six items on O4:\n\n- **Multiple choice (q1, q2, q5):** telling a workflow from an agent by who decides the next step, applied to a makerspace booking flow and to a choice of which request suits an agent.\n- **Numeric (q3):** how many model calls a fixed workflow makes across a day of requests.\n- **Short answer (q4, q6):** one reason to prefer a fixed workflow, and a short argument about whether the training-record check should be a model decision, given the small budget.\n\nThis quiz is ahead of the lessons. You haven't had a lesson on workflows versus agents yet, so it checks the objective itself and uses your makerspace assistant as the running example. I didn't search for a source. The key follows the standard definition that workflows run on predefined code paths and agents direct their own steps, which I wrote from memory.\n\nThe key uses two misconception ids that are new to this workspace, M7 and M8:\n\n- **M7:** treating \"agent\" as the smarter or default choice, or mixing up what separates the two.\n- **M8:** believing a workflow uses no model.\n\nWant a short lesson on this objective before you take the quiz?",
